{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3169","artifact_type":"codebase-analysis","name":"plan/codebase-patterns-duplicate-detection-content-match.md@sha256:3a2bfafa13995ced6874d754a31f5ba239c535159290d374bee9fc5261c31e37"},"owner_reference":"3169","content":"# Codebase Analysis: Duplicate Detection (Issue #3169)\n\n## Patterns & Architecture\n\n### Current Write-Time Validation Structure\n\n#### `backlog_core/operations.py::_check_for_duplicates` (~line 1341)\n**Current behavior:**\n- Single entry point for all duplicate detection\n- Called from `add_item` at line 1503 \u2014 inside item creation, at write time\n- Signature: `_check_for_duplicates(title: str, force: bool) -> None`\n- Returns nothing; raises `DuplicateItemError` if duplicates found\n- Flow:\n  1. If `force=True`, returns immediately (bypass)\n  2. Fetches all existing items via `get_config().backend.list_work_items()` \u2014 cache-only read\n  3. Calls `find_fuzzy_duplicates(title, existing_items)` to run title similarity check\n  4. Raises `DuplicateItemError` if matches found; otherwise returns silently\n\n**When it runs:**\n- Inside `add_item()` at line 1503, called after argument validation but before `BacklogItem` construction\n- Result: by the time the check fires, caller has already invested effort analyzing/formulating the item\n- No path for the caller to *read and act on* the result except abort or force bypass\n\n**Cache-only read risk:**\n- Calls `backend.list_work_items()` without any refresh parameter\n- For `GitHubBackend` (line 184 of `github_backend.py`), delegates to `self._reconciliation.list_work_items()`\n- GitHub backend's docstring (line 179) explicitly states: \"List work items from the provider-private cache\"\n- No `from_github` parameter exposed to the duplicate check\n- Items created by concurrent sessions not yet pulled into local cache are invisible\n- Exception message cannot distinguish \"no duplicate\" from \"could not check\"\n\n---\n\n#### `backlog_core/parsing.py::find_fuzzy_duplicates` (~line 536)\n**Current algorithm:**\n- Pure title-only character-sequence similarity using `difflib.SequenceMatcher`\n- Signature: `find_fuzzy_duplicates(title: str, items: list[BacklogItem], threshold: float = FUZZY_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD) -> list[tuple[str, float, str]]`\n- Returns list of `(existing_title, similarity_ratio, file_path)` tuples sorted by ratio descending\n\n**Processing:**\n1. Normalize new title: strip conventional-commit prefix (feat:, fix:, refactor: etc.), lowercase\n2. For each item in items:\n   - Skip if `item.skip == True` (done/resolved items)\n   - Skip if title is empty\n   - Normalize existing title same way\n   - Calculate `difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, normalized_new, normalized_existing).ratio()`\n   - Append tuple if ratio >= threshold (default 0.80 per `FUZZY_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD`)\n3. Sort by similarity descending\n\n**What it matches on:**\n- Title field ONLY, no description, no acceptance criteria, no body sections\n- Character-sequence similarity, not semantic similarity\n- Two authors describing the same defect with different wording will not match\n- Evidence from issue #3169: \"CI check for drift...\" vs \"Agent `tools:` frontmatter drifts...\" scored 0.4683 (threshold 0.80)\n\n**Constants:**\n- `FUZZY_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD = 0.80` (defined in `backlog_core/models.py`)\n- No other configurable parameters in the function call chain\n\n---\n\n#### `backlog_core/models.py::DuplicateItemError` (line 561)\n**Current shape:**\n```python\nclass DuplicateItemError(BacklogError):\n    def __init__(self, duplicates: list[tuple[str, float, str]]) -> None:\n        self.duplicates = duplicates\n        titles = \", \".join(f'\"{t}\" ({int(r * 100)}%)' for t, r, _ in duplicates)\n        super().__init__(f\"Similar backlog items found: {titles}\")\n```\n\n**What it carries:**\n- `duplicates`: list of `(title, similarity_ratio, file_path)` tuples\n- `message`: human-readable string with matched titles and percentages\n\n**What it does NOT carry:**\n- Existing item's `issue` reference (GitHub number or beads nanoid)\n- Existing item's `reference` field (needed to extend via `groom-backlog-item` etc.)\n- Existing item's `description` or any content for comparison\n- Information about which field matched (all matches appear to come from title)\n\n**When raised:**\n- From `_check_for_duplicates` when matches found\n- Caught by CLI handler (`sam_schema/backlog.py::add` line 72) and MCP handler (`server.py::backlog_add` line 1731)\n- Caught callers see: exception message with titles/percentages, stored on `.duplicates`, but no structured way to fetch the full item\n\n---\n\n### Multi-Backend Protocol: `list_work_items()`\n\n#### `backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py::list_work_items` (line 178)\n```python\ndef list_work_items(self) -> list[BacklogItem]:\n    \"\"\"List work items from the provider-private cache.\"\"\"\n    return self._reconciliation.list_work_items()\n```\n- Reads from cached reconciliation state only\n- No parameters; no `from_github` option exposed here\n- Delegates to `_reconciliation` (a `_GitHubReconciliation` instance)\n- Implementation in `github_work_items.py::list_work_items` (line 437)\n\n#### `backlog_core/backends/sqlite_backend.py::list_work_items` (line 200)\n- Native storage backend; reads from SQLite database\n- Synchronous; no network calls or cache staleness risk\n- Same protocol signature (no parameters)\n\n#### `backlog_core/backends/memory_backend.py::list_work_items` (line 139)\n- In-memory test backend\n- Returns `list(self.items.values())`\n- Same protocol signature\n\n#### `backlog_core/backends/beads_backend.py::list_work_items` (line 269)\n- String-ID backend; reads from beads instance\n- Same protocol signature; no cache-staleness risk (beads is live)\n\n**Protocol invariant:**\n- All backends implement `list_work_items() -> list[BacklogItem]` with no parameters\n- All return only items currently \"known\" to the backend (cached or persisted)\n- Caller must know whether a \"known\" set is fresh or stale before using the result authoritatively\n\n---\n\n### Full-Text Search Engine: `backlog_core/server.py`\n\n#### `backlog_list` MCP tool (line 1935)\n**Parameters relevant to duplicate detection:**\n- `from_github: bool = False` \u2014 when True, refreshes local cache from GitHub before listing\n- `search: str | None = None` \u2014 full-text search query across title, description, acceptance criteria, all section bodies\n  - Supports OR/AND/NOT operators: `'auth OR deploy'`, `'backlog NOT quality'`\n  - Supports regex: `/pattern/` or `regex:pattern`\n  - Supports field-specific search: `title:auth`, `type:bug`, `topic:devops`, `section:P1`, `body:sdlc-layers`\n  - Case-insensitive substring matching as fallback\n  - Operator precedence: NOT > AND > OR\n- `match_context: bool = False` \u2014 when True, returns 'matches' list showing where each search term was found\n  - Includes field name, term, snippet, and section context (e.g. 'body:acceptance-criteria')\n\n**How it works:**\n1. `_tokenize_search(search: str)` (line 391) \u2014 parses search query into tokens and operators\n2. `_apply_search_filter(items: list[dict], search: str)` (line 516) \u2014 evaluates search against each item\n3. Search executes across complete item content including description, sections, body text\n4. Returns items matching the query with optional match context\n\n**Exposure:**\n- Available in MCP via `backlog_list` with `from_github=True` and `search=...` parameters\n- CLI: `backlog list` command does NOT have `--search` option (only `--title` substring filter)\n- `backlog merged-prs` CLI command IS the only CLI command with `--search` support (line 342-344)\n- This is a documented gap per Impact Radius: \"CLI has no `--search` equivalent\"\n\n**How it should be used for duplicate detection:**\n- Extract 2-4 concepts from new item title/description\n- Build OR query from those concepts: `e.g. \"drift OR mcp OR tool-lists\"`\n- Call `backlog_list(from_github=True, search=..., match_context=True)`\n- Results include all items whose content mentions those concepts, with match locations\n- Caller reads results and decides whether to extend or create new item\n- This is the documented workflow in `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` Step 3 (lines 90-110)\n\n---\n\n### CLI Wiring: `sam_schema/backlog.py`\n\n#### `add` command (line 38)\n```python\n@app.command(\"add\")\ndef add(\n    title: str,\n    description: str,\n    priority: str,\n    source: str = \"Not specified\",\n    type_: str = \"Feature\",\n    force: bool = False,\n    repo: str = \"\",\n) -> None:\n```\n- Calls `operations.add_item(...)` with `force` parameter passed through\n- On error, exits with JSON error via `cli_output.exit_with_json_error`\n- Duplicate detection runs inside `add_item`; no pre-write search capability from CLI\n\n#### `list_items` command (line 77)\n- Has `--title` filter (substring match, case-insensitive)\n- Has `--section`, `--status`, `--type`, `--topic` filters\n- Does NOT have `--search` parameter for full-text search\n- Cannot be used to implement the documented Step 3 workflow from CLI\n\n#### `merged_prs` command (line 342-344)\n- Only CLI command with `--search` parameter\n- Demonstrates the pattern exists in CLI but is not exposed for `list_items`\n\n#### No pre-write search path\n- CLI workflow cannot call `backlog list --search` before `backlog add`\n- Users must use MCP or manual workflow to check for duplicates before calling `add`\n\n---\n\n### Integration Points: `backlog_core/server.py`\n\n#### `backlog_add` MCP tool (line 1683)\n```python\nasync def backlog_add(\n    title: str,\n    priority: str,\n    description: str,\n    source: str = \"Not specified\",\n    type_: str = \"Feature\",\n    force: bool = False,\n) -> dict:\n```\n- Calls `operations.add_item(...)` via `asyncio.to_thread`\n- `force` parameter: \"Skip fuzzy duplicate check\" (documented in line 1702)\n- No `from_github` parameter exposed\n- Duplicate detection runs inside `add_item` at write time\n\n**Documented workflow comment (lines 1709-1712):**\n> \"For guided creation with classification and research support, use `/dh:work-backlog-item create` instead of calling this tool directly \u2014 it applies the same description template below plus duplicate detection (also enforced here unconditionally) and item-type classification.\"\n\nThis indicates duplicate detection is meant to be enforced unconditionally, suggesting the current location inside `add_item` is intentional, but the issue's root cause analysis identifies this as a design gap.\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Current Architecture\n\n**Write-Time Validation Flow:**\n```\nCaller \u2192 backlog_add (MCP) or add (CLI)\n  \u2193\noperations.add_item(title, force, ...)\n  \u2193\n_check_for_duplicates(title, force)\n  \u251c\u2500 if force: return (skip)\n  \u2514\u2500 items = backend.list_work_items() [cache-only, no refresh]\n  \u2514\u2500 duplicates = find_fuzzy_duplicates(title, items) [title-only, SequenceMatcher]\n  \u2514\u2500 if duplicates: raise DuplicateItemError([(title, ratio, file_path), ...])\n  \u2193\n(BacklogItem construction + persistence)\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n1. **Timing**: Check runs at write time, after effort is spent\n2. **Algorithm**: Title character-sequence only, not semantic\n3. **Data source**: Cache-only, no refresh option, concurrent writes invisible\n4. **Result shape**: Returns (title, ratio, file_path) \u2014 no item reference, no content\n5. **Exception path**: Only \"abort\" or \"force\" options; no \"extend existing\" path\n6. **CLI coverage**: `--search` not exposed in `list_items` CLI command\n\n---\n\n## Related Architecture Documents\n\n- `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md`: Documents cache invariant \u2014 \"Cache misses are unavailable data, not authoritative empty results\"\n- `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md`: Step 3 specifies search-based detection workflow\n- `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md`: Flow chart describes Step 3 with \"`backlog_list` search/filter, title overlap \u2264 2 token edit distance\"\n- `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`: Auto-generated workflow reference graph with Step 3 duplicate detection node"}